WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.280
Welcome to Grade 2 English, Unit 1: Welcome and Calendar.

2
00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:10.340
You will learn how to say and spell your name, introduce
a partner, and say what people like using like and likes.

3
00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:14.240
You will learn the calendar words too: the days of the week,

4
00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:17.540
the months of the year and the order words we use for dates.

5
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:23.280
You will hunt for English words around your home,
and ask simple questions about colours and numbers.

6
00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:30.560
By the end you will be ready to welcome a new friend, just
as Amal does in this unit's story, “Amal's First Week”.

7
00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:36.460
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

8
00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:43.800
By the end of this unit, you will be able to say and
spell your name, and ask others how to spell theirs.

9
00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:48.220
You will also introduce yourself
and a partner using simple sentences.

10
00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:52.860
You will also say what you and other
people like, using like and likes.

11
00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:55.620
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

12
00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:03.220
Your vocabulary work begins with these
words: train, snail, tail, sail, wait, week.

13
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:08.880
Listen to each word, look at what it means,
and try to use it when you talk and write.

14
00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:15.200
The reading sequence includes Words Around
Us and A Poem: “When I Open Up a Book”.

15
00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:20.860
Read slowly, look at the pictures,
and find the big idea in each text.

16
00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:24.940
When you answer a question, point to the words that show it.

17
00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:29.900
The first language focus is He and She: Choose the Pronoun.

18
00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:35.340
We use he and she so that we do not need
to say a person's name again and again.

19
00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:39.680
Use he for a boy or a man, and she for a girl or a woman.

20
00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:43.820
Look at the examples, then try
the pattern in your own sentences.

21
00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:49.960
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1 — Introduce Yourself.

22
00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:53.560
Say your ideas clearly and listen to your partner.

23
00:01:54.240 --> 00:02:00.360
In writing, you will draw, trace, copy or write,
then check your work with a grown-up or the AI tutor.

24
00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:02.400
You are ready to begin.

25
00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:08.640
Start with the words, then the reading and the
questions, then the grammar, speaking and writing.

26
00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:14.860
Ask the AI tutor for help any time, and bring your
questions to a live session too if you join one.
